# Project progress stats

After shipping a **major** feature or friend-test milestone (not every tiny fix):

1. Update [`plans/project-progress-stats.md`](plans/project-progress-stats.md):
   - Refresh **Snapshot** (`git rev-list --count HEAD`, latest commit time, elapsed from start **2026-09-20 13:41 −04:00**).
   - Add a short bullet under today’s day section (or create a new `### Day N — …` heading).
2. Write **product outcomes**, not raw commit subjects.
3. Skip noise: typos, renames, one-line CSS, plan-only doc tweaks unless they are themselves the milestone.

If the user asks “how long did this take?” or for progress stats, read that file first and refresh the snapshot numbers from git before answering.
